  "notes": "The invalidation arm, pinned through a golden. A shallow (T_IN, WETH) pool sets m_X first and an out-leg is priced at that amount; then the adjacency scan — which only runs once the pump has gone dry — delivers a much deeper in-leg, m_X improves, and the out-leg measured at the old amount is outdated and re-measured at the new one. The log therefore contains the SAME out-leg pool at two different amounts, and the golden is the composition through the second.",
